#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065139} :activity/id #uuid "ec92f9e5-f4ff-5e7d-bf06-75063f0fdeca" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048771 :topic/id #uuid "bd590864-b974-5af1-ab3d-4de57a31118a" :topic/math-academy-id 311} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065139 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065333 :tutorial/content "Let's find the total area of the finite region enclosed between curves the curves\n\n$$\nf(x)=x^3-2x\n$$\n\nand $g(x)=2x$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e6/e651f9df1fbc9f0f9ad8ffa49822e4e3640a3555570ca3d0f82c155c5141843e.png)\n\nFirst, we find the points where the curves intersect:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= g(x) \\\\\nx^{3} - 2x &= 2x \\\\\nx^{3} - 4x &= 0 \\\\\nx(x^{2} - 4) &= 0 \\\\\nx(x - 2)(x + 2) &= 0 \\\\\nx &= 0, 2,-2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area we want consists of two symmetric regions: $A_1$ and $A_2$.\n\n![](images/4f/4fd6173127725bd771a753217002ab9656cf36a97dd37c4fe80f7d76e672ee86.png)\n\nFor the area $A_1$, we have $x \\in [-2,0]$, and the upper function is $f(x)$ while the lower function is $g(x)$. So, the area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA_{1} &= \\int_{-2}^{0}(f(x) - g(x))dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-2}^{0}((x^{3} - 2x) - 2x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-2}^{0}(x^{3} - 4x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int_{-2}^{0}x^{3}dx - 4\\int_{-2}^{0}xdx \\\\\n&= \\left.\\frac{x^{4}}{4}\\right|_{-2}^{0} - 4 \\cdot \\left.\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right|_{-2}^{0} \\\\\n&= (0 - 4) - 4(0 - 2) \\\\\n&=-4 + 8 \\\\\n&= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the regions are symmetric, we have that $A_2=A_1=4$.\n\nFinally, the required area is given by\n\n$$\nA = A_1 + A_2 = 4 + 4 = 8\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "988c723b-81d1-541c-9ab3-bebbece1cf06" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1003 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "3d1d4c5b-f669-5ef8-ae3a-069d89747d69" :step/math-academy-id 1966 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065178}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065140 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064260 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064105 :question/id #uuid "2e0348cd-6ee1-5e95-8164-2edc58084312" :question/math-academy-id "e-558"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ebf33bf5-1693-5ffa-b545-379f5dc60622" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064885} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064886}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Between Two Curves Expressed as Functions of X That Intersect at Three Points"} :step/id #uuid "0b4e1339-dcb7-5439-a531-66ef32ae8045" :step/math-academy-id 1967 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065141}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065141 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064261 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064106 :question/id #uuid "a36dbf41-414c-55e3-a9f6-4b925d571442" :question/math-academy-id "e-559"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf150ae8-865f-5eda-8725-731d4e915873" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050548}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064880} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064882} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527929}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area Between Two Curves Expressed as Functions of Y That Intersect at Three Points"} :step/id #uuid "91fabaf9-366a-5699-bd24-1f3331ce4790" :step/math-academy-id 1971} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065178 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064289 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064130 :question/id #uuid "2a359419-c37d-5772-bf4b-1f2757272ad9" :question/math-academy-id "e-7357"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7f2ec03d-c811-5009-8498-7b5960bc8d0f" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049042} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050551} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050827}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064881} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064884}] :knowledge-point/title "Constructing an Integral Expression That Represents the Area Between Two Curves"} :step/id #uuid "55aedc57-c528-5f39-b05b-126f9ef5cee0" :step/math-academy-id 27313 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065140}}] 